Books I think of when I think of D&D.

Initial list, 2026-08-28
* The Dying Earth series, by Jack Vance.
* The Intercontinental Union of Disgusting Characters, by Roger M. Wilcox.
* The R. A. Salvatore novels about Drizzt Do'Urden and the Forgotten Realms.
* The Theives' World series by Robert Lynn Asprin.
* The stories of Conan the Barbarian by Robert E. Howard.
* The stories of Elric of Melniboné, by Michael Moorcock.
* The stories of Fafhrd and the Gray Mouser by Fritz Leiber.
* The various version of D&D by Gary Gygax and Dave Arneson.
* Three Hearts and Three Lions, by Poul Anderson.
* The Hobbit and The Lord of the Rings, by J.R.R. Tolkein.
